<!-- Documentation: https://www.jetbrains.org/intellij/sdk/docs/basics/plugin_structure/plugin_configuration_file.html -->

<!-- url="" specifies the URL of the plugin homepage (displayed in the Welcome Screen and in "Plugins" settings dialog) -->
<idea-plugin url="https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/wikis">

    <!-- Unique identifier of the plugin. Cannot be changed between the plugin versions. If not specified, assumed to be equal to <name>. -->
    <id>net.javaru.idea.frc</id>
    <name>FRC</name>
    <version>replacedAtBuildTime</version>

    <!-- The vendor of the plugin.
       The optional "url" attribute specifies the URL of the vendor homepage.
       The optional "email" attribute specifies the e-mail address of the vendor. -->
    <vendor url="https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin" >Javaru</vendor>

    <!-- please see https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/build-number-ranges.html for description -->
    <idea-version since-build="*.*" until-build="*.*"/>

    <description><![CDATA[
        <p>
            <!-- The first sentence gets used as a summary at the JetBrains Plugins Repository. -->
            <em><a href='https://www.firstinspires.org'>FIRST</a> Robotics Competition</em>
            (<a href='https://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/frc'>FRC</a>) development support for
            IntelliJ IDEA, including new project wizards, new class templates, robust RioLog console,
            and more. Enjoy using your favorite IDE when coding your team's robot in Java
            and/or Kotlin.
        </p>
        <p><br></p>
        <p>
            <strong>Please report issues or make feature requests via the project's</strong>
            <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues'>Issue Tracker</a>.<br>
            This is an unofficial plugin written by an FRC team mentor. Please do <em>not</em>
            contact <em>FIRST</em> or the WPI Lib developers for support. Use the above link. Thanks.
        </p>
    ]]></description>

    <change-notes><![CDATA[
        <strong>v2.0.0</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Support for 2022 season, including project templates<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; New Project Wizard: Added Kotlin based new project templates<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; New Project Wizard: Added option to include Kotlin support in projects<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.6.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Resolves a potential NPE<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.6.0</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Numerous internal refactoring and improvements<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Complete rewrite of Gradle interaction for improved user experience, and to resolve
                           <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/94'>issue #94</a>,
                           an occasional thread access issue on gradle re-import.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; FRC oriented custom icons for some directories in Project tool window. (Can be disabled via
                           <em>Settings/Preferences &gt; Languages &amp; Frameworks &gt; FRC &gt; &quot;Provide custom icons in project view&quot;</em>) <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Removed support for legacy Ant based FRC projects<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; FRC Project Wizard: Resolved an issue with gradle run configurations still using the old shared run
                           configurations directory rather than the newer <tt>{projectRoot}/.run</tt> directory.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added IntelliJ IDEA v2021.3 support.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.5.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Miscellaneous internal refactoring and improvements<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; This is the last release for IntelliJ IDEA 2020.2, 2020.3, and 2021.1. IntelliJ IDEA 2021.2 or newer will be required 
                           for the next FRC Plugin release, which will support the 2022 FRC Season. Please see the
                           <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/-/blob/master/README.adoc#eol-policy'>FRC Plugin's EOL Policy</a> 
                           for more detail.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.5.0</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added action link to "WPI Lib update available" notification to automatically update the gradle build file to use the new version<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Improved Romi projects support in New Project Wizard. It now creates some additional Romi specific Run Configurations including
                           Shuffleboard and Smart Dashboard launch configs.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Some additional work towards migrating the FRC Plugin to be a dynamic plugin (i.e. restart of IDEA not required after upgrading FRC plugin).<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Refactorings to remove use of a number of methods and classes recently deprecated in the IntelliJ IDEA Plugin API.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Refactorings to remove use of a few items recently marked as "Internal Use Only" in the IntelliJ IDEA Plugin API.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Resolves <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/87'>issue #87</a>, FRC Tool Window name shows long name in 2020.3<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Resolves <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/84'>issue #84</a>, WPI Lib root path not discovered on Mac or Linux<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Resolves <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/92'>issue #92</a>, a Dispatch Thread access issue on opening an FRC project in IntelliJ IDEA v2021.1<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Resolves a corner case issue in the Command creation template in which the rules to determine if a Subsystem was a singleton or not were a bit too strict<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; 1.5.0-2021.2 only: Refactorings to remove use of a number of methods and classes deprecated in the IntelliJ IDEA Plugin API in v2021.2.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.4.0</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Support for IntelliJ IDEA v2020.2 and later only. See the
                           <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/-/blob/master/README.adoc#eol-policy'>FRC Plugin's EOL Policy</a> for more detail.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; FRC Project Wizard: Updated Project Templates for 2021 to match the WPI Lib ones. This included adding the new Romi projects.
                           Also added the Romi Reference example template. However, the other example templates still need to be check for any
                           potential updates. An an initial look seems to indicate the changes made for 2021 are mostly superficial.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; FRC Project Wizard: Gradle run configurations are now stored in <tt>{projectRoot}/.run</tt> rather then <tt>{projectRoot}/.idea/runConfigurations</tt>
                           (as introduced in IntelliJ IDEA v2020.1) for easier/better sharing of run configurations.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; FRC Project Wizard: .idea files are now ignored by default in .gitignore rather than shared as the default.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; FRC Project Wizard: Improved auto import of gradle project upon project creation.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Preparation for migrating the Plugin to be a dynamic plugin (i.e. restart of IDEA not required after upgrading FRC plugin).
                           Full Dynamic Plugin capabilities are planned for a near future release.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Some minor improvements to the Subsystem singleton templates.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Replaced use of deprecated IntelliJ IDEA Plugin APIs with new APIs.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Updated FRC/WPI spell check dictionary with new domain specific words introduced in 2021.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Miscellaneous internal improvements.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.3.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; <strong>This is the last release for v2019.2, v2019.3 and v2020.1. The next release will only support
        IntelliJ IDEA v2020.2 and later. See the <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/-/blob/master/README.adoc#eol-policy'>FRC Plugin's EOL Policy</a>
        for more detail.</strong><br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Miscellaneous internal improvements.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.3.0</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; This is a re-release of v1.2.1 but as v1.3.0. Due to the lack of a patch level indicator in the
                           v1.2 release, the IntelliJ IDEA plugin frameworks was not seeing v1.2.1-2020.1 as being newer than
                           v1.2-2020.1 and therefore not auto updating to it. Moving forward, all releases will have a patch level
                           configured to prevent this issue.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.2.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Fixed <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/64'>issue #64</a> in which a plugin
                           'State Error' exception may have occurred on IDE startup.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.2</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Enhanced the Subsystem "Create as Singleton" option to offer different Singleton initialization
                           methodologies (based on the methodologies presented in the <em>Geeks for Geeks</em>
                           <a href="https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/singleton-design-pattern">Singleton Design Pattern</a> article).<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added functionality to Command class creation so that Subsystems that are Singletons are not added
                           as parameters to the Command's constructor, but rather are initialized in their field declaration
                           via a call to their singleton getter method (or field if applicable).<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Enhanced the Command class creation dialog so that abstract subsystem classes are not listed in
                           the "required subsystems" selection pane. Since an abstract subsystem cannot be instantiated, it
                           made no sense to present them as an option in the list.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Enhanced the component creation dialogs so that the last selected base component is remembered
                           and pre-selected on the next use.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Implemented <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/63'>Feature #63</a>:
                           Auto reimport gradle project when changes are made to <em>vendordeps</em> directory so that changes are
                           picked up and the project classpath is updated appropriately.
                           (<a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/61'>Feature #61</a>, UI for
                           adding and managing <em>vendordeps</em>, is still pending.)<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Some miscellaneous internal improvements.<br>
        <br>

        <strong>v1.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added an action (<em>Tools > FRC > Check for WPI Lib Update</em>) to check for the availability of a WPI Lib update. The action runs
                           automatically when an FRC project is opened, and then periodically in the background while the FRC project is open.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Fixed the auto clear feature in the rioLog console tool window. It was keying on an old startup message and thus not working.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Removed the print action from the rioLog console. It was likely never used and was using real estate and adding clutter.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Rearranged the order of the action buttons on the rioLog console so that the more frequently used actions are
                           on the top to improve usability when the tool window height is reduced.<br>
        <br>

        <strong>v1.0</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Dropping the zero based versioning and migrating to a 1.0 version after 14 such releases over the course of three years.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Improvements to the new FRC Robot Project Wizard<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Wizard automatically creates Gradle build and deploy Run Configurations, as well as debugger attachment Configurations.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added 2020 project and example templates.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; The wizard checks for the latest WPI Lib version so new projects always can use the latest version.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; RioLog Console reads team number from project level rather than application level.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added JSON Schema Validation for the wpilib_preferences.json file. This prevents errors and provides auto completion.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Major rewrite of the FRC class creation template framework to make them more robust and convenient.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Additional words added to the FRC spellcheck dictionary.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Miscellaneous changes and improvements<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Deprecated the custom FrcModuleType used by the custom FRC Project Wizard and instead have the wizard create JavaModuleType projects.
        This change will have very minimal impact to users, but improves some functionality. See <a href="https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/41">Enhancement #41</a>
        for additional details.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Good luck to all FRC teams in the 2020 <em>INFINITE RECHARGE</em> game.<br>
        <br>

        <strong>v0.1 - v0.8.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Fourteen early development releases over three years containing numerous features, enhancements, and fixes.
    ]]>
    </change-notes>


